@startuml
!theme plain

title ssh-proxy Managed Runtime Lifecycle

actor User
participant "ssh-proxy CLI" as CLI
control "Managed daemon" as Daemon
participant "/usr/bin/ssh" as SSH
boundary "SOCKS5\n127.0.0.1:1080" as SOCKS
boundary "HTTP forward proxy\n127.0.0.1:8080" as HTTP

autonumber

== Start ==

User -> CLI: ssh-proxy start
CLI -> Daemon: spawn selected profile
Daemon -> Daemon: acquire profile lock\nrecord starting state
Daemon -> SSH: start -D 127.0.0.1:1080
SSH -> SOCKS: bind dynamic forward
Daemon -> SOCKS: SOCKS5 greeting probe

alt SOCKS5 ready
  SOCKS --> Daemon: version 5 / no-auth accepted
  Daemon -> HTTP: bind only after SOCKS readiness
  alt HTTP listener ready
    HTTP --> Daemon: ready
    Daemon -> Daemon: atomically record daemon PID,\nSSH PID, endpoints, up state
    Daemon --> CLI: ready
    CLI --> User: SOCKS and HTTP endpoints
  else HTTP bridge startup fails
    Daemon -> HTTP: close if partially opened
    Daemon -> SSH: SIGTERM and wait
    Daemon -> Daemon: remove state and lock
    Daemon --> CLI: start failed
  end
else SSH exits or SOCKS probe fails
  Daemon -> SSH: SIGTERM and wait if alive
  Daemon -> Daemon: remove state and lock
  Daemon --> CLI: start failed
end

== Stop ==

User -> CLI: ssh-proxy stop
CLI -> Daemon: request shutdown
Daemon -> Daemon: record stopping state
Daemon -> HTTP: close listener and active relays
HTTP --> Daemon: closed
Daemon -> SSH: SIGTERM and wait
SSH --> Daemon: exited
Daemon -> Daemon: remove current state and lock
Daemon --> CLI: stopped
CLI --> User: connection down

@enduml
